# {{senseid|en|cycling}} {{lb|en|transitive|cycling}} To cause a [[collision#Noun|collision]] by opening the door of a vehicle in front of an [[oncoming#Adjective|oncoming]] [[cyclist#Noun|cyclist]] or [[pedestrian#Noun|pedestrian]].
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Helen Pidd|title=I got 'doored' while undertaking on my bike. Was it my fault?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230815141137/http://www.theguardian.com/environment/bike-blog/2018/feb/06/i-got-doored-while-undertaking-on-my-bike-was-it-my-fault|date=6 February 2018|passage=Kerr has acted for numerous clients who have been '''doored''', including one man knocked off his bike and on to spiked railings, and another who ended up hitting a tree.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Ben Spurr|title=How an Ontario rule stops 'doored' cyclists from getting drivers' insurance info|work=w:Toronto Star|url=https://www.thestar.com/news/gta/how-an-ontario-rule-stops-doored-cyclists-from-getting-drivers-insurance-info/article_feb75ac5-ea06-5870-9880-bc7b0054f1da.html|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/Q2gxa|archivedate=27 April 2024|location=Toronto, Ont.|publisher=w:Toronto Star Newspapers Ltd.|date=15 December 2019|issn=0319-0781|oclc=1081127642|passage=He [Pete Karageorgos] said cyclists who are '''doored''' are entitled to claim accident benefits from the driver's insurer if they aren't covered by a policy of their own.}}
#* {{RQ:LATimes|author=Angie Orellana Hernandez|title=Being doored to death is a cyclist's nightmare. How can it be prevented?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240422034231/https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2023-12-19/what-is-dooring-the-bicyclist-collision-that-killed-a-hollywood-producer|date=19 December 2023|passage=To avoid being '''doored''', cyclists such as Vilain, Davis-Overstreet and Michael Schneider monitor as many telltale signs as possible: shadows, brake lights, the actions of people sitting in the driver's seat.}}

